WEBVTT

00:36.028 --> 00:37.154
Lois, look at this.

00:37.321 --> 00:40.825
My essay won first prize in the
New England Rising Writers contest.

00:40.992 --> 00:43.619
I'm gonna be honored at the ceremony
on Martha's Vineyard.

00:43.786 --> 00:46.038
Ooh, New England Rising Writers.

00:46.205 --> 00:49.125
I'm sure it'll be a veritable
who's that of the literary world.

00:49.291 --> 00:50.334
Laugh all you want...

00:50.501 --> 00:53.379
...but they're gonna put me up
at a luxury hotel, all expenses paid.

00:53.546 --> 00:56.799
- Wow, congratulations, Brian.
- Meg, please, I'm talking.

00:56.966 --> 01:00.094
Over a thousand people entered
the contest and they chose mine.

01:00.261 --> 01:03.514
- Well, that's wonderful, Brian.
- Yeah, that's a great achievement.

01:03.681 --> 01:07.601
Just like the first chemotherapy patient
to figure out the handkerchief look.

01:09.812 --> 01:12.231
- Honey, get in here.
WOMAN: What is it?

01:12.398 --> 01:13.732
Just... Just get in here.

01:13.898 --> 01:16.025
What? Oh, my God.

01:16.192 --> 01:17.819
- Right?
- It's like you...

01:17.986 --> 01:20.780
...don't even have cancer. Oh, my God.
- Don't even have cancer. I know.

01:20.947 --> 01:22.198
[CHUCKLING]

01:22.365 --> 01:24.993
No, but I still have
pretty aggressive cancer.

01:28.037 --> 01:31.666
Come on, Peter, we're gonna be late
for lunch with Mom and Dad.

01:31.833 --> 01:34.169
Oh, right.

01:34.335 --> 01:37.005
- You didn't forget, did you?
- No, no, I didn't forget.

01:37.172 --> 01:40.175
Let me just go change
out of this fishing gear.

01:41.718 --> 01:44.554
- Hey, Peter, what's up?
- Come on, we gotta go now. Come on.

01:44.721 --> 01:46.598
Joe, Joe, Quagmire.
Come on. Go, go, go.

01:46.764 --> 01:48.725
Pull the car around. Come on, let's go.

01:48.892 --> 01:50.477
[PHONE RINGS]

01:50.977 --> 01:53.480
<i>- Hello?
PETER: Lois, this is Peter.</i>

01:53.646 --> 01:56.900
<i>I'm afraid that on my way
to the bedroom to change, I took ill.</i>

01:57.066 --> 01:58.735
<i>You'd best go to lunch without me.</i>

01:58.902 --> 02:02.322
<i>- Why do I hear an engine?
- My stomach is rumbling in a way...</i>

02:02.489 --> 02:05.074
<i>... that sounds like the engine
of Joe's fishing truck.</i>

02:05.241 --> 02:07.744
<i>- Peter, are you lying?
- Oh, now she's a doctor, guys.</i>

02:07.911 --> 02:09.287
<i>QUAGMIRE: Hi, Lois.
PETER: Quagmire says hi.</i>

02:09.454 --> 02:11.789
Damn it, Peter, you're going fishing,
aren't you?

02:11.956 --> 02:14.292
You promised you'd come to lunch
with my parents.

02:14.459 --> 02:16.628
<i>Lois, until we get
an appointment secretary...</i>

02:16.794 --> 02:19.964
<i>... things like this are gonna continue
to fall through the cracks.</i>

02:20.131 --> 02:22.133
My parents are not
gonna like this, Peter.

02:22.300 --> 02:25.011
They're still angry
at how you behaved at our wedding.

02:26.345 --> 02:32.142
- You may now kiss the bride.
- Kiss her? I am gonna destroy her.

02:37.397 --> 02:39.942
Mom, are you still mad at Dad
about yesterday?

02:40.108 --> 02:43.612
Well, sort of. I mean,
we planned that lunch two weeks ago.

02:43.779 --> 02:47.407
But he promised he'd go with me to put
flowers on my grandmother's grave...

02:47.574 --> 02:50.744
...so I guess it's all right.
Peter, are you ready?

02:50.911 --> 02:53.956
Oh, right.

02:57.709 --> 03:00.671
So a lot of tension
with Peter lately, huh?

03:00.837 --> 03:04.424
That's an understatement, Brian.
He's been incredibly thoughtless lately.

03:04.591 --> 03:08.220
Even more so than usual.
But tonight is our sex night...

03:08.387 --> 03:11.556
...and a little physical release
will do us both some good.

03:11.723 --> 03:14.643
- Peter, are you? Oh, come on!
- Lois, I know it's late...

03:14.810 --> 03:16.979
...but me and the guys
were going beekeeping.

03:17.145 --> 03:19.356
Oh, my God.
What the hell is wrong with you?

03:19.523 --> 03:24.111
Whoa, someone just yelled themselves
out of honey with breakfast.

03:24.277 --> 03:25.612
I don't need honey, Peter...

03:25.779 --> 03:28.323
...I need a husband
who wants to spend time with me.

03:28.490 --> 03:30.033
Can I make a suggestion?

03:30.200 --> 03:33.412
All you two have done is argue
about stuff for the past two weeks.

03:33.578 --> 03:35.414
It's my guess
you could use a vacation.

03:35.580 --> 03:37.416
Why don't you come
to Martha's Vineyard...

03:37.582 --> 03:38.916
...and watch me accept my award?

03:39.417 --> 03:43.129
- Wow, does that sound wonderful.
- Whoa, whoa, that sounds expensive.

03:43.295 --> 03:46.757
Can't we just do something fun
here at the house? It's just as relaxing.

03:46.924 --> 03:50.428
Hey, guys, I've decided
I'm gonna take up the drums.

03:50.928 --> 03:53.431
- I'll start packing.
- I'll start packing.

03:53.597 --> 03:56.642
[LAUGHING]

04:06.652 --> 04:09.905
Quagmire, we're only gonna be in
Martha's Vineyard for a couple days.

04:10.072 --> 04:11.741
Can't you just watch the kids?

04:11.907 --> 04:15.119
Oh, man. You're more of a letdown
than Fruit Stripe gum.

04:16.787 --> 04:18.789
Mm. Aw.

04:19.081 --> 04:22.460
What are we gonna do? Quagmire's busy,
and Joe and Bonnie are out of town.

04:22.626 --> 04:23.961
Well, what about Cleveland?

04:24.128 --> 04:26.464
He's on the road
touring with Black Box.

04:27.256 --> 04:29.133
[BLACK BOX'S
"EVERYBOD Y EVERYBOD Y" PLAYING]

04:31.177 --> 04:36.348
[SINGING]

04:39.018 --> 04:42.313
Wait a minute. What about that
nice old man who lives up the street?

04:42.480 --> 04:44.523
Oh, yeah.
Maybe Herbert can watch the kids.

04:44.690 --> 04:46.567
He seems like a responsible guy.

04:46.734 --> 04:48.402
So it would only be till Monday...

04:48.569 --> 04:51.447
...and we could pay you for it.
- It's real easy, I promise.

04:51.614 --> 04:54.073
I mean, you've spent time
watching children, right?

04:54.240 --> 04:57.160
- Yes, sir. Yes, I have.
- Wonderful.

04:57.327 --> 04:58.870
You mind stopping by
tomorrow morning?

04:59.037 --> 05:01.414
I'll wear my snazziest duds.

05:03.166 --> 05:07.378
<i>[SINGING] Got my tweed pressed
Got my best vest</i>

05:07.545 --> 05:12.091
<i>All I need now is the boy</i>

05:12.258 --> 05:16.513
<i>Got my striped tie
Got my hopes high</i>

05:16.679 --> 05:19.724
<i>Got the time and the place
And I got rhythm</i>

05:19.891 --> 05:22.143
<i>Now all I need
Is Chris to go with 'em</i>

05:22.310 --> 05:25.647
<i>If he'll
Just appear we'll</i>

05:25.813 --> 05:30.527
<i>Fill this big town
Full of joy</i>

05:30.693 --> 05:35.281
<i>And if he'll say, "My darling I'm yours"
I'll throw away</i>

05:35.448 --> 05:39.702
<i>My striped tie
And my best-pressed tweed</i>

05:39.869 --> 05:44.791
<i>All I really need
Is a boy</i>

05:56.719 --> 06:00.223
Brian, this is wonderful.
I feel like one of the Kennedys.

06:00.390 --> 06:04.435
The overprivileged drunk ones,
not the socially responsible dead ones.

06:04.602 --> 06:06.478
This resort offers wonderful amenities.

06:06.645 --> 06:09.731
They have birdwatching,
wine tasting, horseback riding.

06:09.898 --> 06:11.775
Hey, they also have stork startling.

06:13.151 --> 06:15.612
[IMITATES BIRD CALL]

06:15.779 --> 06:21.618
Ha-ha-ha-ha! Your bird intelligence
is no match for my people intelligence.

06:25.289 --> 06:30.794
- Ah, this is so wonderfully peaceful.
- Yeah, it really is another world out here.

06:30.961 --> 06:32.754
And just so quiet.

06:32.921 --> 06:35.424
<i>Heh-heh-heh-heh-heh-heh
Heh-heh-heh-heh-heh-heh</i>

06:35.590 --> 06:37.467
<i>I'm half shark
And half Peter</i>

06:37.634 --> 06:39.303
<i>Don 't come near me
I will eat you</i>

06:39.469 --> 06:41.471
<i>Heh-heh-heh-heh-heh
Heh-heh-heh-heh-heh</i>

06:41.638 --> 06:43.849
Peter, will you knock that off?
It's getting annoying.

06:44.016 --> 06:46.101
All right, fine. I'm gonna go
scare some people.

06:46.268 --> 06:49.062
Heh. Nobody'll buy it.
There are no sharks out here.

06:49.229 --> 06:53.358
Lots of people swimming up there.
I could pig out if I wanted to.

06:53.525 --> 06:55.027
But I'm watching my weight
because...

06:55.193 --> 06:57.571
...I don't wanna spend
the Fourth of July alone again.

06:57.738 --> 07:02.075
Plus, I ate a dog yesterday and now
I got a bone stuck in my anus.

07:04.828 --> 07:07.247
All right, children,
your mammy and pappy...

07:07.414 --> 07:10.459
...asked me to look after you
for the next couple days.

07:10.625 --> 07:13.253
So I wanna lay down
a few ground rules.

07:13.420 --> 07:15.714
No cussing, clean your plates...

07:15.881 --> 07:19.592
...and only a half-hour of radio
and then it's off to bed.

07:19.759 --> 07:22.344
- Well, that sucks.
- And don't you mouth off to me...

07:22.511 --> 07:24.972
...or I'm gonna slap you
right in your penis.

07:25.139 --> 07:28.976
No offense, Mr. Herbert, but I'm a
17-year-old girl and I don't need you here.

07:29.143 --> 07:30.686
Well, no offense to you, Meg...

07:30.853 --> 07:34.774
...but you're a 17-year-old girl,
and I don't need you here.

07:40.029 --> 07:41.906
What do you think is keeping Peter?

07:42.072 --> 07:44.575
I hope he gets here
before they give you your award.

07:44.742 --> 07:47.119
Well, you're here, Lois,
that's enough for me.

07:47.286 --> 07:50.372
Oh, you always know just what to say.

07:50.539 --> 07:53.876
And the award for Most Mediocre
Children's Book goes to:

07:54.043 --> 07:56.629
<i>The Adventures of Haskell:
The Mystery Horse.</i>

07:56.796 --> 07:58.714
Here to accept is Haskell.

07:58.881 --> 08:00.591
[APPLAUSE]

08:00.758 --> 08:04.053
Thank you.
Where am I gonna go next?

08:04.220 --> 08:08.057
What interesting adventure?
You don't know.

08:08.224 --> 08:10.184
I'll have my award now.

08:11.227 --> 08:12.937
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

08:13.103 --> 08:16.524
And now, reading a passage from his
grand prize-winning short essay...

08:16.690 --> 08:20.528
..."Amazing Grace," tonight's
guest of honor, Mr. Brian Griffin.

08:24.073 --> 08:25.825
Thank you very much.

08:25.991 --> 08:29.245
"She was Grace,
in name and in essence.

08:29.411 --> 08:34.207
To those she loved, she exuded
strength, life, laughter and light.

08:34.374 --> 08:36.459
And to me, also sorrow...

08:36.626 --> 08:39.212
...for circumstance had bound her
to my best friend...

08:39.379 --> 08:42.966
...through whom we met
in the warmth and serenity of her home.

08:43.132 --> 08:45.009
Nothing from the first day I saw her...

08:45.176 --> 08:47.345
...and no one
that has happened to me since...

08:47.512 --> 08:50.682
...has ever been as frightening
and as confusing.

08:50.848 --> 08:53.309
For no person I've ever known
has ever done more...

08:53.476 --> 08:57.897
...to make me feel more sure,
more insecure, more important...

08:58.064 --> 09:00.441
...and less significant."

09:08.116 --> 09:10.118
That was beautiful, Brian.

09:10.285 --> 09:13.621
Well, you know what they say,
write what's in your heart.

09:13.788 --> 09:17.750
Hey. Did... Did I miss Byron's reward?

09:17.917 --> 09:20.920
Brian's award. And yes, you did, Peter.

09:21.087 --> 09:25.800
You've been a good son, Brian.
And I'm sorry you're so sick.

09:25.967 --> 09:28.303
- What?
- Peter, where the hell have you been?

09:28.469 --> 09:32.140
Every time you... We go to a hotel...

09:32.307 --> 09:34.976
...you hide the key
to the minibar from me.

09:35.143 --> 09:37.520
But I found it.

09:37.687 --> 09:39.564
[WHISPERS]
I found it.

09:39.731 --> 09:42.483
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Lois. Griffin.

09:42.650 --> 09:46.153
You're a piece of work, you know that?
An hour late and you're drunk.

09:46.320 --> 09:49.406
You had an opportunity
to share a beautiful moment with Brian...

09:49.573 --> 09:50.699
...and you wasted it.

09:50.866 --> 09:53.702
Wasted it like the Osmond family
wastes water.

09:54.703 --> 09:56.955
Who's in the shower? Is it Donny?

09:57.122 --> 09:59.583
No, I showered earlier.
It could be Merrill.

09:59.750 --> 10:02.336
- Merrill's right here.
- Well, where's Jimmy?

10:02.502 --> 10:04.963
Jimmy's running through the sprinklers
in the yard.

10:05.130 --> 10:07.799
- Is it Marie?
- No, no one's in there.

10:07.966 --> 10:11.011
So the shower's just running
with no one in there?

10:11.178 --> 10:14.723
- That's right.
- Well, I'll be a son of a gun.

10:17.768 --> 10:19.728
[SNORING AND DOOR KNOCKS]

10:19.978 --> 10:23.315
- Hey, good morning.
- Oh, good morning, Brian.

10:23.482 --> 10:26.651
Oh, that's a lovely fragrance
you're wearing. What is it?

10:26.818 --> 10:29.571
Oh, this?
This is Hartz Mountain Flea Dip.

10:29.738 --> 10:32.532
Kills ticks, fleas and mosquitoes.
It's very potent.

10:32.699 --> 10:35.077
Almost as potent
as the inspiration you give me...

10:35.243 --> 10:37.412
...to plumb the deepest fathoms
of my soul...

10:37.579 --> 10:41.249
...for a literary bounty
of truth and loveliness.

10:41.416 --> 10:43.251
[FARTING]

10:43.710 --> 10:46.922
Ahh, that's so much better.

10:47.422 --> 10:48.715
Morning, Lois.

10:48.882 --> 10:51.968
I'm sorry about last night.
I promise I'll make it up to you.

10:52.135 --> 10:54.096
Well, if you really mean that...

10:54.262 --> 10:56.598
...I was hoping
we could go paddle boating today.

10:56.765 --> 10:59.391
Great. But can we do it after 5?
There's a ballgame on.

10:59.558 --> 11:01.936
Oh, well, then,
maybe Brian and I can hang out.

11:02.102 --> 11:04.271
- Do you mind, Brian?
- No, not at all.

11:04.438 --> 11:06.690
Good. Can you move?
You're blocking the screen.

11:06.857 --> 11:10.778
<i>MAN 1: We now return to
Damn, Nature, You Scary! on BET.</i>

11:10.945 --> 11:13.739
<i>MAN 2: Damn, that motherfucker
run fast. You see that shit?</i>

11:14.240 --> 11:16.742
<i>That thing come by my house,
I'll kill it.</i>

11:17.076 --> 11:18.786
[GROWLS]

11:19.245 --> 11:23.791
<i>That little rat-looking thing just got ate!
Damn, nature, you scary.</i>

12:56.466 --> 12:58.676
- Y'all know what day it is?
BOTH: No.

12:58.843 --> 13:02.263
- It's bath day.
- Oh, I don't wanna take a bath.

13:02.430 --> 13:03.514
[CHUCKLES]

13:03.681 --> 13:06.601
Not for you, silly. It's bath day for me.

13:06.768 --> 13:08.603
But I can't wash myself.

13:08.770 --> 13:11.481
Know anybody
with a pair of strong young hands...

13:11.647 --> 13:13.733
...to help me in and out of the tub?

13:14.359 --> 13:16.819
Oh, rats.

13:20.490 --> 13:22.658
I had so much fun today, Brian.

13:22.825 --> 13:25.452
So did I. Hey, you feel like
grabbing something to eat?

13:25.619 --> 13:26.661
Oh, I'd love to...

13:26.828 --> 13:30.707
...but Peter and I, we're gonna
get dinner at that little place by the...

13:36.713 --> 13:40.759
Well, heh, looks like I am free.
Hey, you know what might be fun?

13:40.926 --> 13:44.262
How about we just order room service
and watch a couple of bad movies?

13:44.429 --> 13:47.182
<i>Yeah, that does sound like fun.
I'll go rent Vanilla Sky.</i>

13:47.349 --> 13:50.268
I said a bad movie, not an abortion.

13:53.146 --> 13:55.565
This is gonna be great.
A whole evening with Lois.

13:55.732 --> 13:57.234
We are gonna have a fun time.

13:57.400 --> 13:58.443
Lois, my darling.

13:58.610 --> 14:01.363
A couple of steaks, some wine,
maybe a couple of sundaes.

14:01.530 --> 14:02.614
Lois, my darling.

14:02.781 --> 14:04.491
A little music, some candlelight.

14:04.658 --> 14:05.742
Lois, my darling.

14:05.909 --> 14:08.203
Whoa, whoa, whoa, what am I doing?

14:08.370 --> 14:10.038
This is Lois, Peter's wife.

14:10.205 --> 14:12.582
How can I even think about
trying anything?

14:12.749 --> 14:13.834
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

14:14.000 --> 14:15.418
<i>- Hello?
STEWIE: Hey, Brian, it's me.</i>

14:15.585 --> 14:18.880
<i>I got a question for you.
Herbert and I are playing Scattergories...</i>

14:19.047 --> 14:22.425
<i>... would you count NyQuil as a beverage?
- Um...</i>

14:22.592 --> 14:23.635
<i>- No, right?
- No.</i>

14:23.802 --> 14:25.887
<i>Yeah, not gonna fly, old man.
Thanks, Brian.</i>

14:26.054 --> 14:28.265
<i>HERBERT:
Oh, that is bullshit.</i>

14:32.185 --> 14:35.063
- This is so much fun, Brian.
- Well, it's a Saturday night...

14:35.230 --> 14:37.857
...sorry the video-store pickings
were a little sparse.

14:38.023 --> 14:39.400
<i>Hope you like Roman Holiday.</i>

14:39.567 --> 14:42.736
<i>Tee-hee. I lied.
I was a princess the whole time.</i>

14:42.903 --> 14:46.282
<i>You bitch.
I'm gonna punch you in the face.</i>

14:46.782 --> 14:50.703
That was a lovely dinner.
I saved all my scraps in a bag for you.

14:50.870 --> 14:52.371
Thanks.

14:52.538 --> 14:55.833
You know, Lois, I'm sure
you've already figured this out...

14:56.000 --> 14:57.626
...but that essay I wrote...

14:57.793 --> 15:00.212
...I wrote it about you.
- Aw.

15:00.796 --> 15:02.381
I had a hunch.

15:02.548 --> 15:05.843
Thank you, Brian.
I'm glad you shared that with me.

15:06.010 --> 15:08.429
Well, you know, Lois,
you mean a lot to me.

15:08.596 --> 15:11.348
I mean,
things you say and things you do...

15:11.515 --> 15:13.392
...resonate with me in a big way.

15:13.559 --> 15:15.561
When you drive away
to go to the market...

15:15.728 --> 15:17.563
...I don't know
what to do with myself.

15:17.730 --> 15:20.733
Then when I hear that car coming up
the driveway, I go berserk.

15:20.899 --> 15:24.820
I mean, half the time when you go to the
market, I assume you're leaving forever.

15:24.987 --> 15:26.655
And when you get back I realize...

15:26.822 --> 15:29.617
...I have no idea
how long you've been gone and I...

15:29.783 --> 15:31.869
Well, you know what, I'm rambling.

15:32.036 --> 15:35.539
- Would like some more champagne?
- I'd love some.

15:36.790 --> 15:39.752
Oh, my head is swimming.

15:41.128 --> 15:43.297
Oh, my God, Brian, no!

15:43.464 --> 15:46.383
- Stop it! What are you doing?
- I can't help myself, Lois.

15:46.550 --> 15:50.219
I know you're married to Peter, but
I love you and I can't stand it anymore.

15:50.386 --> 15:53.723
Brian, no! No! Get down! Get down!

15:53.890 --> 15:55.642
This is a good sweater!

15:55.808 --> 15:58.353
Off! Off!

15:58.519 --> 16:00.647
Brian, I think you'd better go.

16:08.154 --> 16:10.531
Lois, I'd really like to talk about this.

16:10.698 --> 16:11.824
[BRIAN SCRATCHING DOOR]

16:11.991 --> 16:14.660
- No! Stop scratching the door!
- Okay.

16:19.207 --> 16:20.833
Oh, my God, I attacked Lois.

16:21.000 --> 16:23.044
What the hell was I thinking?
I'm a rapist.

16:23.211 --> 16:26.881
I'm no better than
Kobe Bryant or Mike Tyson or Reagan.

16:27.048 --> 16:28.216
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

16:28.383 --> 16:30.385
<i>STEWIE: Hey, Brian.
Another Scattergories question.</i>

16:30.551 --> 16:34.138
<i>The category is "type of pet."
Herbert put Cambodian.</i>

16:34.305 --> 16:35.473
<i>That's not right, right?</i>

16:35.640 --> 16:37.642
Look, Stewie,
I can't talk about this now.

16:37.809 --> 16:39.185
Jeez, what's your problem?

16:39.352 --> 16:43.856
I just... I did a bad thing
and I don't know what to do about it.

16:44.023 --> 16:46.025
I feel like I'm losing my mind.

16:46.192 --> 16:48.694
That's how I felt at that
Grateful Dead show.

16:48.861 --> 16:51.906
Does anybody want to buy my shirt?

16:52.115 --> 16:55.034
I'll trade you my shirt
for a grilled cheese.

16:55.201 --> 16:59.080
So, what happened, sport?
Come on. Talk to your pal, Stewie.

16:59.247 --> 17:02.291
All right, but only because
I've gotta tell somebody.

17:02.791 --> 17:05.502
I pretty much
just threw myself at Lois.

17:05.669 --> 17:08.046
So you finally did it, huh?

17:08.213 --> 17:09.965
Well, look, Brian, as your friend...

17:10.132 --> 17:12.926
...I should tell you that
that vagina is ground zero, man.

17:13.093 --> 17:15.762
I mean, I just...
I wrecked that thing on the way out.

17:15.929 --> 17:19.766
And just to be a jerk,
I carved "Brooks was here" in the wall.

17:19.933 --> 17:22.978
Did you see that?
Did you see "Brooks was here"?

17:23.145 --> 17:24.187
We didn't have sex.

17:24.354 --> 17:28.066
Of course, what with Chris before me,
I pretty much just walked out of there.

17:28.233 --> 17:29.734
Didn't even have to stoop over.

17:29.901 --> 17:32.445
There was even room
to twirl a cane as I strolled.

17:32.612 --> 17:34.656
- You're exaggerating.
- Only a little bit...

17:34.823 --> 17:36.449
...that's the messed-up thing.

17:40.370 --> 17:42.289
- Morning, Lois.
- Peter, there you are.

17:42.455 --> 17:44.749
Were you down at that hotel bar
all night again?

17:44.916 --> 17:48.128
I was. And you know who's
staying at this hotel? Nathan Lane.

17:48.295 --> 17:51.381
We got wasted at the bar and
he ended up asking me to marry him.

17:51.548 --> 17:54.968
So I convinced this minister to do
the job, but the joke's on Nathan...

17:55.135 --> 17:58.722
...because gay people can't get married.
- They can in this state, Peter.

17:58.889 --> 18:02.642
Oh. Well, in that case,
we're registered at Filene's.

18:02.809 --> 18:05.854
God, you've spent
half this entire trip intoxicated.

18:06.021 --> 18:07.898
Oh, I'm intoxicated all right, Lois...

18:08.064 --> 18:10.692
...by the beauty and magic
of Martha's Vineyard...

18:10.859 --> 18:14.237
...Nantucket, Cape Cod
and all the great destinations...

18:14.404 --> 18:17.156
...that make Massachusetts
the wondrous place it is.

18:34.924 --> 18:37.092
I am so glad
Brian brought us out here, Lois.

18:37.259 --> 18:39.011
He's a real pal, you know that?

18:39.178 --> 18:41.972
Well, it's actually Brian
I need to talk to you about.

18:42.139 --> 18:44.099
Boy, he's a hell of a guy, isn't he?

18:44.308 --> 18:47.478
I mean, Quagmire's a lot of fun at a
party, but he's so horny all the time...

18:47.645 --> 18:50.230
...I feel like I can't trust him.
Cleveland's a great guy...

18:50.397 --> 18:53.150
...but he's got a moustache,
so you gotta wonder what he's hiding.

18:53.317 --> 18:57.154
Joe's a cripple, so for obvious reasons
I can't trust him. But Brian...

18:57.321 --> 19:00.783
Brian's solid.
He's the one guy I know I can trust.

19:00.949 --> 19:03.952
Brian tried to have sex with me.

19:04.703 --> 19:06.372
Was he bigger than me?

19:09.500 --> 19:12.670
"And they told Peter
to stay away from the wolf.

19:12.836 --> 19:16.674
But he didn't listen to them
because he's his own man.

19:16.840 --> 19:21.220
And he knew that sometimes the things
that seem the most dangerous...

19:21.387 --> 19:23.931
...turn out to be the most fun."

19:24.098 --> 19:27.768
Yes, sir, it was a good day
for young Peter.

19:27.935 --> 19:30.978
[WHISTLING "PETER AND THE WOLF"]

19:37.860 --> 19:39.445
Are you a pedophile?

19:46.202 --> 19:49.497
Hey, uh, Lois told me
there was some funny business.

19:49.664 --> 19:51.416
- Yeah, what of it?
- Well, it's just...

19:51.582 --> 19:53.876
I can't help but feel
a little betrayed, Brian.

19:54.043 --> 19:55.503
Lois is my wife and...

19:55.670 --> 19:58.381
I mean, all the dry food
I bought for you over the years?

19:58.548 --> 20:01.050
- Yeah, well, you don't deserve her.
- Say what now?

20:01.217 --> 20:02.260
You don't deserve her.

20:02.427 --> 20:04.595
She does nothing
but give and give and give...

20:04.762 --> 20:07.140
...and you repay her
with selfishness and neglect.

20:07.306 --> 20:10.309
You've barely spent any time
with her at all on this vacation.

20:10.476 --> 20:12.645
Who are you to tell me
how to run my marriage?

20:12.812 --> 20:15.481
You can't hang onto a girlfriend
for more than a couple months.

20:15.648 --> 20:19.402
- What the hell is that supposed to mean?
- You're a train wreck with that crap.

20:19.569 --> 20:24.282
You couldn't get Jillian to take you back
and she was dumber than Lou Ferrigno.

20:26.200 --> 20:28.411
[GROWLING]

20:38.796 --> 20:40.381
[GROANS]

20:41.883 --> 20:43.717
[GRUNTING]

20:54.978 --> 20:57.772
Stop it! Stop it! Get off my husband!

20:57.939 --> 21:01.026
Wait a minute, Brian.
Nathan Lane is right.

21:01.193 --> 21:03.904
- What are we doing?
- Look, I'm sorry, all right?

21:04.070 --> 21:07.657
It's just... When you have feelings
for someone that are strong enough...

21:07.824 --> 21:11.745
...you just, I don't know,
lose sight of the rest of the world.

21:11.912 --> 21:16.041
Brian, she's my wife.
And you're my best pal.

21:16.207 --> 21:18.168
So, what are we gonna do about this?

21:19.210 --> 21:23.465
I promise, Peter,
nothing like this will ever happen again.

21:23.965 --> 21:25.258
Thanks, old buddy.

21:25.425 --> 21:28.094
Yeah, blah, blah, blah,
that's all well and good, Peter.

21:28.261 --> 21:31.640
Now, get ready, we're having dinner
with my parents tonight.

21:31.806 --> 21:35.060
Oh, right.

21:38.855 --> 21:41.232
I just feel terrible
about this whole thing, Lois.

21:41.399 --> 21:45.528
- Can you ever forgive me?
- Yes, Brian, I can.

21:45.695 --> 21:47.781
But there's something
you deserve to know.

21:47.948 --> 21:50.075
- What's that?
- Well...

21:50.241 --> 21:52.535
...it's not like
I haven't thought about it.

21:52.702 --> 21:54.079
- Really?
- Well, yes.

21:54.245 --> 21:56.789
I mean,
you and I have a lot in common...

21:56.956 --> 22:00.292
...and we've spent so much time
together over the years...

22:00.459 --> 22:02.544
...and of course
that essay you wrote...

22:02.711 --> 22:04.630
...it really touched my heart.

22:04.797 --> 22:06.131
Well, to be honest, Lois...

22:06.298 --> 22:09.593
<i>...I ripped off most of that speech
from Summer of '42.</i>

22:09.760 --> 22:12.554
Oh. Well, it was still nice.

22:12.721 --> 22:13.972
Let me just ask you this.

22:14.139 --> 22:17.184
When these thoughts about you and I
have crossed your mind...

22:17.351 --> 22:20.396
...is it good?
- What do you mean?

22:20.562 --> 22:22.439
Well...

22:22.606 --> 22:23.649
- Oh.
- Yeah.

22:23.816 --> 22:27.695
Well, a lot of times when Peter and I
are having sex, I feel suffocated.

22:27.861 --> 22:31.490
But with you, I imagine it would be
like doing it with a stuffed animal.

22:31.657 --> 22:33.075
Everybody ready to go?

22:33.242 --> 22:35.327
- All set, Peter.
- Good.

22:35.494 --> 22:37.371
We may be
leaving Martha's Vineyard...

22:37.538 --> 22:39.623
...but the spirit
of this wonderful place...

22:39.790 --> 22:43.085
...will stay in our hearts
all the way home. Because, after all...

22:43.836 --> 22:47.506
<i>[SINGING] The spirit of Massachusetts
Is the spirit of America</i>

22:47.673 --> 22:51.260
<i>The spirit of what's old
And what's new</i>

22:51.427 --> 22:55.139
<i>The spirit of Massachusetts
Is the spirit of America</i>

22:55.305 --> 22:59.184
<i>The spirit of the red, white and blue</i>

22:59.351 --> 23:03.063
<i>The spirit of Massachusetts
Is the spirit of America</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:06.859
<i>The spirit of what's old
And what's new</i>

23:07.025 --> 23:10.528
<i>The spirit of Massachusetts
Is the spirit of America</i>

23:10.695 --> 23:17.869
<i>The spirit of the red, white and blue</i>

23:29.464 --> 23:32.508
[SNORING]

24:36.030 --> 25:37.030
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru